    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1608": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Marketing",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Marketing Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Marketing Assistant Professor in Marketing SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics : Type of contract : p ermanent contract, full-time contract Start Date : From August 2027 Loca tion : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Lille (one position) ; SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Sophia Antipolis (one position) SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the Market Interactions Research Cent r e invite applications for positions in Marketing to begin in August 202 7 . The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the goal of publishing in the field's top-tier journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a selection criterion . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include: Having recently (preferably within the last 3 years) completed, or being about to complete, a Ph.D. in Marketing from a world-class institution. Research interest and publications relate d to one or more of the following domains : consumer behavior, consumer culture theory, digital marketing, branding , international marketing, sustainable marketing, marketing ethics, and modeling . Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research in marketing in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in marketing . Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in marketing and Supervise master students. Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the school’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School , mentioning your campus of choice * . Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider relevant. Details and Deadline for applications: The application should be submitted in English by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject , in accordance to the choice of campus : “Application for Position in Marketing – France , Lille” or “Application for Position in Marketing – France , Sophia Antipolis” * . The application package should be submitted as a single PDF document . The deadline for applications is November 30, 2026 . Review of applications will begin in October 2026 and continue until the position is filled . * Candidates may apply for one position only and will remain associated with their selected campus throughout the entire recruitment process . Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications from candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH AT MINT The successful candidate will be a member of the Market Interactions (MINT) research centre . Market Interactions Research Centre (MINT) investigates the complex and evolving dynamics between market agents, consumers, and society. Research at MINT revolves mostly around three interlinked themes: ( 1) Stakeholder Interactions: the study of interactions among diverse market actors, including consumers, organisations , institutions, and communities; (2) Material Interactions: t he study of how humans engage with objects, technologies, and material environments in social settings and the marketplace ; (3) Moral Interactions: The study of ethical, political, and moral framings that govern market interactions. For further information: Market Interactions | SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL #WeAreSKEMA Rejoignez-nous ! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1609": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business Assistant Professor Position in Artificial Intelligence for Business SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job charasteristics Type of contract : P ermanent contract, full time contract Taking office : F rom August 202 7 Localisation : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Sophia Antipolis campus. SKEMA Business School ( https://www.skema.edu/ ) and the SKEMA Center for Artificial Intelligence ( Skema Center for Artificial Intelligence ) i nvite applications for a position at the rank of Assistant Professor in Artificial Intelligence for Business , to begin August 2027. The successful candidate will develop and/or lead academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field's highest quality journals. The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications should include: Hold or about to complete a Ph.D. in Management or a related field (with orientation in Artificial Intelligence, Business Analytics, Robotics) or a related area (preference will be given to a candidate who will complete their Ph.D. by August 202 7 ). Strong evidence of recent research productivity and/or demonstrable potential to publish research in journals highly ranked on the CABS-FNEGE-FT50 lists. Teaching excellence in Ai for Business or related fields. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in the area of Artificial Intelligence for Business , with a focus either in strategy and innovation or in organizational behavior and human resources management . Supervise master students . Show academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to the projects related to the school’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity (1-2 writing samples or reference to research available online; published articles or working papers). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be submitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “application position in ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE FOR BUSINESS – FRANCE” Applications will be reviewed from September until December 31, 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’ Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The candidate s will be member s of the SKEMA Center for Artificial Intelligence (SCAI), a research centre dedicated to exploring how AI Systems interact and collaborate with people to enhance human abilities and empower both individuals and society creating sustainable value at four different levels : Business value : how AI becomes part of the products themselves, improves performance across the value chain, or enables ecosystems and collaboration with new markets. Ethical value : how to foster explicability and responsible AI to guarantee social fairness in respect of human freedoms and dignity. Societal value : how AI contributes to environmental sustainability, encourages a new social contract based on accountability. Algorithmic value : developing AI techniques and algorithms with increasingly superior performance while attending to the explainability of such techniques to assure that the other kinds of value can be enabled. Through this Research Centre, we want to analyze the impact of Artificial Intelligence on a broad range of business and management subjects (ranging from finance, marketing, strategy, to innovation and entrepreneurship) and cover a multitude of different sectors (such as education, energy, health care, public administration, banks, insurance, retail, tourism, and luxury) offering guidance to organizations on how to best use AI for sustainable value creation. For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
    },
    "https://recrutement.skema.edu/?page=advertisement_display&id=1610": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Accounting",
      "description": "Skema BS e-recruiting | Nos offresAssistant Professor in Accounting Bienvenue dans l'espace recrutement eRecruiting Nos offres d'emploi / détails de l'offre Nos offres d'emploi retour Assistant Professor in Accounting Assistant Professor in Accounting SKEMA | AT HOME WORLDWIDE* *Chez vous, partout dans le monde Job characteristics: Type of contract : Permanent contract, full-time contract. Taking office : From September 2027. Localisation : SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL Sophia Antipolis campus. SKEMA Business School (https://www.skema.edu/) and the Finance & Accounting Insights on Risk and Regulation (FAIRR) research center invite applications for assistant professor positions in finance to begin August 202 7 . The successful candidates will develop academic research projects with the aim of publishing in the field ’ s highest quality journals. We encourage applications from scholars with a focus on quantitative research in financial accounting . The school offers a vibrant research environment with strong established groups, including in the finance and accounting area, and is seeking to reinforce existing expertise . The position is permanent with a full-time contract. Salary and conditions are competitive, in line with international standards. SKEMA Business School offers publication bonuses for peer-reviewed publications. The language of work and teaching is English. Knowledge of French is not required and is not a criterion for selection . SKEMA Business School offers support in learning French. Qualifications must include: A Ph.D. in Accounting or a related field. Promising research prospects, visible through a high-quality pipeline of papers targeting top - level journals, in areas consistent with the specializations of current f aculty members. Initial teaching experience in the relevant disciplinary area. Ability to work as part of a team in a collegial environment. Strong oral and written communication skills . Commitment to service and/or outreach activities commensurate with the rank of assistant professor. Expectations: Publish peer-reviewed publications in top-tier journals. Teach courses in accounting and related fields . Supervise master and/or bachelor students. Demonstrate academic citizenship, commit to the life of the institution, and contribute to projects related to the s chool’s strategy. Applications should include: A letter of application stating why you are interested in SKEMA Business School Curriculum v itae. Statement of research interests and direction. Statement of teaching interests and philosophy (please list courses you have taught or would prefer to teach). Evidence of research activity ( published articles or working papers ). Evidence of teaching performance ( include teaching evaluations if available). Three letters of reference. Any additional document that the applicant may consider as relevant. The application should be s ubmitted in English and sent by email to recruitmentfaculty2027@skema.edu , with the following subject : “ A pplication position in FINANCE - FRANCE ”. Applications will be reviewed from September until December 31, 2026 or until the position is filled. Please note that SKEMA is an equal opportunity employer, which values all types of diversity, and encourages applications of candidates from all backgrounds. ABOUT SKEMA BUSINESS SCHOOL With 11,000 students of 130 nationalities and 60,000 alumni in 145 countries, SKEMA Business School is a global school that trains and educates the talents that 21st-century business requires through its research, its 70 teaching programs, and its international multi-site structure. The school currently has campuses in France (Lille, Sophia Antipolis, Paris), China (Suzhou and Nanjing), the United States (Raleigh), Brazil (Belo Horizonte), UAE (Dubai ) and South Africa (Stellenbosch). The school is also developing an Innovation Center in AI (Canada), one of the world's major AI hubs. SKEMA’s Faculty comprises more than 190 Professors, organized by Academy – Globalization, Innovation, Transformation, and Digitalization – and Research Centers. SKEMA is multi-accredited - EQUIS, AACSB, EFMD EMBA Accredited. Its programs are recognized in France (Visa, ‘ Licence Degree ’, Master Degree , RNCP, CGE label), as well as in the United States (Licensing), Brazil ( Certificação ), and China (Ministry of Education). Member of the Conférence des Grandes Ecoles (CGE). Member of the Conférence des Directeurs d’Ecoles Françaises de Management (CDEFM). For further information: https://www.skema.edu/ ABOUT RESEARCH The successful candidate will be part of the FAIRR Research Center, which is dedicated to producing high-quality academic research in Finance and Accounting. The research center comprises about 25 faculty members in finance and accounting and PhD students. FAIRR members are particularly focused on developing high-level expertise in the areas of digital finance, entrepreneurial finance, governance, intermediaries, corporate restructuring, disclosure, financial regulation , and household finance alongside other corporate finance, market finance and accounting topics. We organize regular research seminars on the three French campuses, host international workshops and conferences , and run a PhD program with a dedicated Finance & Accounting track. Our researchers have access to a wide range of databases, including WRDS (CRSP, Compustat , WorldScope , ISS, IBES...), DealScan , SDC, Datastream , Pitchbook, etc. Our members have presented their papers at academic and professional conferences and international institutions. Their work has led to publications in top-ranked journals in finance, accounting, management, economics and entrepreneurial finance (including American Economic Review, Economic Journal, Entrepreneurship Theory and Practice, Journal of Business Venturing, Journal of Corporate Finance, Journal of Economic Theory, Journal of Finance, Journal of Financial and Quantitative Analysis, Journal of Financial Economics, Journal of Financial Intermediation, Management Science, Quarterly Journal of Economics, Review of Accounting Studies, Review of Finance , and Review of Financial Studies). For further information : https://www.skema.edu/en/finance-accounting-insights-risk-and-regulation #WeAreSKEMA Join Us! © 2026 Skema BS e-recruiting Nos offres d'emploi Conditions d'utilisation Protection des données Utilisation des cookies"
